WEBVTT

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.610
Isn't there something you can do, Saotome?!

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:07.710
Is there nothing you can do, Saotome?!

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.710
Kazuya...

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:13.840
<i>If I don't do something, then all of their...</i>

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.050
Rena...

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:23.350
<i>...all of their memory programs will be erased!</i>

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.060
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:34.320
Kazuya, there's one chance.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.330
Transfer the virus out of the others and into me.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.800
According to Totaro, the virus won't infect me, so...

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.140
So, please, Kazuya, use me to save the others!

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.190
Yes! That's the best choice to make!

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.430
The virus won't hurt her!

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:09.350
But, transferring the virus data from all the others into you...

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:13.020
Right, there isn't enough capacity.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.300
It'll be okay.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.660
What's this?

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.290
Oh! That's right!

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:33.040
Every cyber doll has a secret empty block of memory!

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.600
You called it the "free blank memory data space," right?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.380
Anyway, it's there and it's empty, so we can store the data in there!

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.540
You can't just jam stuff into May! Right?

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.930
It <i>is</i> empty, right?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.170
Y-Yeah!

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.680
May, what's in that space?

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.440
Rena! Rena!

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.730
Kazuya, it's no use.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.070
I can't get their fevers down.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.260
What do we do?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.450
Sara!

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.510
Anyway, take Cyber Doll May, load the virus in, give it a spin,

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.470
and then we win!

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.410
Saotome, if we do what that jerk says,

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.120
are you sure May won't be in any danger?

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.090
If anything happened to May, I'd...!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.590
She'll be fine! Saotome, show us!

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.090
Show us how your MAID system has evolved!

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.310
My...

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:22.590
MAID system?

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.850
I'll do my best! For all the others,

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.610
and for you, Kazuya...

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:28.850
I'll do my best!

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:47.080
<i>It's no use! This machine isn't powerful enough to keep up with the virus infection!</i>

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.860
<i>Nanbara, please hurry!</i>

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.010
That's a strange face for me to have.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:09.040
Today, I'm giving my best!

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.150
MY BEST, YOU HEAR ME?!

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.440
The cyber dolls are running out of time!

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:48.430
Please, Kazuya, sir...

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.490
Kazuya?

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.110
Right.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.170
Okay. May, are you ready?

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:47.450
Yes. Ready when you are.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:48.920
Here we go.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.360
May!

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.810
May! May.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.650
She's got a fever. Bring me some ice!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:30.850
R-Right!

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:34.480
Kazuya, at this rate, May will also...

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.950
I'm okay.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.700
I'm all right. Thank you, Kasumi.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:47.420
Rena and Kei and Sara and Mami are all trying their best. Also,

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.170
Ikariya, too,

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:51.590
and Nanbara and Totaro,

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.260
and Kazuya.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.760
Everyone's trying their best.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.540
So I'll do my best, too!

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.490
<i>Even if it means...</i>

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.950
Hang in there, May.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:27.630
Right.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:29.490
It's hot.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.250
You're just making it feel worse!

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.260
Oh, it's so cool now. So much better...

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.850
Gimme! Gimme! Gimme!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.440
Huh? This?

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.310
Cripes, why does a squid-bot need to sweat, anyway?!

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.560
Thank you!

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:46.610
No ice left.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.140
Now what?

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.860
Yes?

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.140
What the...?

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.620
That just about covers six months worth of rent.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:06.820
What the...?!

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.420
What is it, Saotome?!

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.430
<i>Welcome to Nanbara's room!</i>

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.320
Huh? What's going on?

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:19.180
Huh? What? Me? That's me!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.140
<i>That's right!</i>

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:22.980
<i>That time when...!</i>

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:33.640
What I say is the password!

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:38.330
<i>I have to do what I did last time. And if I succeed, then...!</i>

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:45.160
Hold it, you made this thing. Can't you do something about it?!

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:47.290
Uh, well, that is...

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.080
My specialty's talking, not typing, so...

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.890
Oh, I know! My descendant, Totaro!

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:54.170
You're not a smooth talker, like me,

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:56.950
but being from the future, this'll be a cinch for you!

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.100
If you want a fast typist, go ask Takuya Saotome!

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.100
"Takuya" Saotome?

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.760
My name is Kotaro.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.690
That's it, Saotome! Go! Go!

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.590
A rich and gentle nice guy!

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:13.670
Kazuya Saotome doesn't have any money!

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.070
From here to eternity, he'll always be poor!

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.590
Nanbara is distinguished! Saotome will be extinguished!

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:20.530
Come on and type, Saotome! C'mon! Don't be an idiot!

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.330
Keep at it! That's the way, Saotome!

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:25.990
May...

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.290
Thank you very much.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:53.190
Kazuya!

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.380
What's wrong, Saotome!

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:55.960
Don't give up Saotome!

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.780
This is no time to choke!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:01.610
Stand up! Stand up! Stand up! Stand up! SAOTOME!

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.920
Are you all right, Kazuya, sir?

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.390
It's you.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.970
Kazuya...

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.560
That's it! Type! Type! Type!

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:36.600
Since I was born, my dream has been to head a huge company that runs the world!

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:39.490
But the shallow dream of my rival Saotome has been...

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.490
...to build Doraemon!

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:43.700
<i>Good... bye... virus!</i>

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:19.490
Rena!

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.740
Ikariya!

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:24.870
I could have sworn...

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.990
Oh, my, my, my. I must be...

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.750
in heaven?

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.320
Oh, I wanna eat some ramen!

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:33.440
Voila!

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.680
Special Nanbara ramen, for just such an occasion.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:38.260
ARE YOU EVEN LISTENING TO ME?!

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:39.510
Nope. Not a word.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:43.770
Hey, you always wait till the most dramatic moment before you appear

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:45.720
and steal the spotlight.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:49.800
Thank goodness. Everyone's well again.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:52.660
Right, Kazuya?

00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:57.740
May?

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.170
May!

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.290
Are you all right, May?!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.030
May!

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:06.240
May! May!

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:10.700
I'm all right.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.110
Man, that was too close for comfort.

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:22.100
I was the one who almost ended up looking horrified.

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:25.280
Doesn't it bother you that <i>your</i> virus caused all this?

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:29.490
Oh, my. Well, a happy ending calls for tasty Nagoya hotaru squid.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:33.130
I thought hotaru squid was a Toyama specialty.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:37.840
Kasumi, you didn't use the time we were all knocked out to do stuff with Kazuya, did you?

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:39.650
There was no time for that.

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:44.150
Still, I'm so glad. Everyone's better now.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.930
I told you so!

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:49.370
Putting it into that blank memory space didn't hurt her at all!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.330
You loaded that virus into <i>there?!</i>

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:54.330
Oh, no...

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.080
What? Is something wrong with her memory now?

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.170
Memories. You mean... there were memories in there?

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:04.420
What's wrong? I'm perfectly fine...

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:05.930
Master.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:28.740
I am a cyber doll, a copyrighted product of the Cyberdyne Corporation.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:36.150
Customers must abide by the Terms of Use agreement in order to use a cyber doll.

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:41.480
If the customer disagrees with the Terms of Use, he must cease use of the cyber doll and return it,

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:47.830
and all included attachments, to the Cyberdyne Corporation.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:52.720
Cyber, what's going on?!

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.810
Cyber Doll May's memory has been reinitialized.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:59.520
Reset to the default mode.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:04.070
Everything but her standard data has been erased.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.180
All her memories from since she met Kazuya,

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:09.920
the good memories she created with all of you, have been erased.

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:11.280
Kazuya...

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:21.330
May treasured the memories she acquired since meeting Kazuya.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:25.130
She wouldn't let them go. She wouldn't let them be erased.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:27.670
Those warm memories she had...

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.000
Me, too.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:34.680
I have so much fun with Kazuya and May and Ikariya and everyone here.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:38.580
It's been so much fun. That's why I treasure them so much.

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:39.690
So much...

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:43.310
I realized it for the first time when I accessed May.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:46.890
How the ordinary things I recorded,

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:50.110
the ordinary memories I had...

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:53.160
were things to be valued.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:59.910
"It doesn't matter if you're a human or a cyber doll when you help people," huh?

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:01.560
What's that?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.040
My memory.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.380
Of something Kazuya Saotome said to me.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:10.210
How typical of Mr. Kazuya...

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:13.140
How so? What do you mean?

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:17.390
"It doesn't matter if you're a human or a cyber doll when you help people."

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:21.580
He honestly views them not as servants, but as equals to accept,

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:26.190
with feelings in their hearts that should be respected.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.490
The black box of the MAID system,

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:36.160
the free blank memory data space was included so that they'd have room to develop those feelings.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:40.960
Cyber Doll May chose to purge them from herself.

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:46.040
All to save the memories in the other cyber dolls.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:47.960
It's all right!

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.170
It's still inside her!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.470
The thing Kazuya wanted so much to create is still in her!

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:56.470
Yes, master?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.440
Uh, well, that is...

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:02.450
There's so much I want to talk to you about,

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:06.860
but I'm just not sure how to say it right.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:09.360
You <i>never</i> know what to say, Saotome!

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.280
Nanbara!

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.390
Your stupid small talk is just going to bore May!

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:18.370
Oh, my, my, my. We won't let her be bored, will we?

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:22.520
May, "Whirlwind of Love 2" will be starting soon.

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.380
We have to review part 1 before it starts, okay?

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:28.150
And I'll help wash the dishes, too!

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:29.000
Okay.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:36.160
In time and space, there is knowledge,
will power, physical strength, endurance,

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:40.140
avoidance, accuracy, behavior, and experiences to master.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:43.670
May, let's experience as many things together as we can!

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:44.400
Okay.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:49.240
May, I caused a lot of trouble for you.

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:52.150
For that, I'll treat you to some ramen next time. On Nanbara's tab.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:58.380
With my Nanbara special talk as background music, I'll treat you to a feast!

00:16:58.380 --> 00:16:59.870
Sara will just get one bowl, though.

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:00.680
Okay.

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:06.820
Oh, my, my, my, May dear. You still have a lot to learn about cleaning and washing and cooking.

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:10.300
Developing real Japanese spirit means you must learn from the past.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:11.190
Okay.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.030
Yo!

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:16.870
Look how many people care about you.

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:20.760
Old memories are nice, but let's go out and make some wonderful new ones, too!

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:24.100
Wonderful memories...

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:28.150
Your memories are inside all of us, too.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.760
Memories with everyone...

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:22.870
The thing I want to create wouldn't be worth it if everyone wasn't included.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:24.510
You have to be with us, May.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.280
Be with you...

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.980
Because, between all of us...

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:34.730
Between all of us...

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.490
...are many more memories to make.

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:40.190
Many more!

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:43.200
May.

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:48.210
Kazuya!

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.710
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:58.040
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:01.260
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:07.810
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:18.040
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.480
Go! Go!

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:24.840
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:31.120
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:38.130
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:42.510
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.930
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:49.050
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:52.560
is a memory I carry with me.

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:55.920
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:59.270
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:02.690
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:08.580
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.720
And... action!

00:21:29.980 --> 00:21:33.000
Please remember, Yamazaki!

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:36.110
Impossible!

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:39.180
M-Mika...

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:45.320
Yamazaki!

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.340
CUT!

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:49.320
What's going on?! Why is this squid here?!

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:51.330
I'm sorry!

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.690
Excuse me!

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:57.220
I asked Ikariya to catch the butterfly for us!

00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:58.290
We're sorry!

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:01.290
The landlord is responsible for the tenants,

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:06.030
and as the famously beautiful daughter of the landlady, I beg your pardon!

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:08.630
I always watch "The Whirlwind of Love!"

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:11.770
I'm sorry! Truly! Please forgive me!

00:22:11.770 --> 00:22:13.390
All I know is that it wasn't May's fault!

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:14.940
It wasn't my fault, either!

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:17.510
Hi, I'm Sara, customer service.

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:20.800
You can't work while you're so upset.

00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:22.260
We should have lunch now.

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:23.360
So, could we all eat lunch...

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:24.220
...together?

00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:27.900
Oh, my, my, my. After all, they say that even when soldiers don't eat, they still eat plates, right?

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:31.440
And we spent all night making lots of food.

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:34.370
Let these lunches make up for that little accident.

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:36.690
PRETTY PLEASE?

00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:41.170
All right. Break for an hour!

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.090
Let's have lunch!

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:44.420
YAY!

00:23:07.630 --> 00:23:11.070
I was able to check if things were okay on my end, too.

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:14.250
Who would've thought a cyber retrovirus would develop?

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:17.470
We owe you a lot, Kazuya, sir. Thank you very much.

00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:20.840
Huh? Yeah, well, uh...

00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:22.920
You don't have to be so polite, you know.

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:27.870
But the truth is I'm a lot younger than you are, sir.

00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:29.660
I told you, <i>you</i> have to speak politely to <i>me!</i>

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:32.730
What? You! You don't even know <i>how</i> to talk nicely!

00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:35.360
What?! You mean <i>you</i> don't! You're very nicely not nice!

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:37.040
Neither one is very polite.

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:38.210
Oh, my, my, my...

00:23:38.210 --> 00:23:42.040
"Very nice" is a compliment, so why are they?

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:46.150
Kazuya!

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:47.750
We got the milk!

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:49.650
It tastes really good, too!

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:51.300
Coming!

00:23:54.980 --> 00:23:58.340
<i>Mr. Kazuya, the wish of "If only I could make that..."</i>

00:23:58.340 --> 00:24:01.960
<i>From that wish, everyone begins to build,</i>

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:04.270
<i>building the various dreams they have.</i>

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:06.790
<i>Working hand in hand with others to create the feelings they share.</i>

00:24:06.790 --> 00:24:08.380
Cheers!

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:10.130
<i>Yes, that's right.</i>

00:24:10.130 --> 00:24:13.250
<i>Because you can't shake another hand when you're all alone.</i>

00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:15.540
What the...?

00:24:15.540 --> 00:24:16.580
Could it be?

00:24:16.580 --> 00:24:17.490
No way!

00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:20.640
Shikishima?

00:24:26.460 --> 00:24:28.860
Wow! May, you're little again!

00:24:29.110 --> 00:24:29.660
It's May!

00:24:29.660 --> 00:24:29.980
May here!

00:24:29.980 --> 00:24:30.750
I'm May~

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:31.510
May here!

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:32.490
Mayshu!

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:32.780
Uh...

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:36.530
And together, we are... Maid Rangers May Five!

00:24:36.530 --> 00:24:37.770
I think you're overdoing it.

00:24:38.680 --> 00:24:40.450
"Never give up!"
